Subject: [PATCH] ufs: qcom: propagate Hibern8 exit failures after clock scaling

The post-change callback discards ufshcd_uic_hibern8_exit() failures and
reports success to the UFS core. On SM8475 the first failure is a Hibern8
exit power-control status 5, followed by an attempted gear 1 to 4 change
on the already broken link and an eventual root filesystem I/O failure.

Return the existing Hibern8 exit result so clock scaling can report the
failed transition instead of proceeding as if it succeeded. Preserve the
underlying error log, recovery and clock-scaling rollback behavior.
This fixes error propagation; it does not claim to cure the link failure.

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -2031,7 +2031,7 @@
 		}
 
 		ufs_qcom_icc_update_bw(host);
-		ufshcd_uic_hibern8_exit(hba);
+		return ufshcd_uic_hibern8_exit(hba);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
